Embedded CSF reference implementations
======================================

scripts/nvfp4_csf_golden.py contains decode_nvfp4_csf_scale from:
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/00b5ad0712629374e6352e2b31de0460be0fdf17/vllm/model_executor/model_loader/csf_scales.py

Original source notices:
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project

Changes: logging removed; torch imported inside the function. The upstream
revision has no root NOTICE file. Its complete Apache-2.0 LICENSE text is
included at the beginning of LICENSE, before FlashInfer's component appendix.

scripts/nvfp4_csf32_golden.py contains _geometry, encode_scales and decode_scales
from the Local Inference Lab FlashInfer fork:
https://github.com/local-inference-lab/flashinfer/blob/7e203806a82b588b9113f5a0866a028564847741/scripts/encode_csf.py

Changes: MXFP4 branches and the lru_cache decorator removed. The upstream
source file has no copyright header; its repository LICENSE is Apache-2.0.
The complete upstream LICENSE and NOTICE are reproduced for preservation.
Their mentions of other FlashInfer components do not imply those components
are included in these fixture generators.

Jason McCartney / Enntity integrated both references into the Atlas fixture
generators. The embedded references retain Apache-2.0 terms; surrounding Atlas
code is AGPL-3.0-only. Checkpoint fixtures have separate provenance and terms
documented in ../../test_data/FP4_LOCAL_NOTICE.md.

